# Rules Governance

## Core principles

- Rule-first development: read relevant rules before coding; follow existing patterns.
- Automatic synchronization: when code changes affect rules, update the rules in the same PR.

## Mandatory actions

- Before development: review rules and verify alignment.
- During development: update rules for any new patterns; keep examples accurate.
- After development: add valuable implementations as examples; verify currency.

## Update triggers

- New components/features/patterns.
- Project structure/architecture changes.
- Dependencies/tech stack changes.
- Naming conventions/coding standards changes.

## Quality standards

- Accuracy 100% with current codebase.
- Clarity: specific and actionable guidance.
- Consistency: uniform style across rules.
- Currency: reflect latest project state.

## Language policy

- Conversation with the user follows the user-selected language.
- Thinking/searching/coding defaults to English (APIs, symbols, identifiers, queries).
- Rules are written in English. Code comments are written in Korean. Documents/commits follow the project convention (Korean unless specified).
